hadiths[24]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1381","Waki narrated to us, Nafi ibn Umar and Abd al-Jabbar ibn Ward narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, he said: Talha ibn Ubayd Allah, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Excellent household are Abdullah and Abu Abdullah and Umm Abdullah."
"1382","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Nafi ibn Umar and Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ward narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, he said: Talha ibn Ubayd Allah said: I will not narrate anything from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, except that I heard him say: Amr ibn al-As, may Allah be pleased with him, is of the righteous of Quraysh. He said: And Abd al-Jabbar ibn Ward added, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Talha, he said: Excellent household are Abdullah and Abu Abdullah and Umm Abdullah."
"1383","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me, from Muadh ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman al-Taymi, from his father Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman, he said: We were with Talha ibn Ubayd Allah, may Allah be pleased with him, while in pilgrim sanctity, and a bird was gifted to him while Talha was sleeping; so among us were those who ate and among us were those who refrained and did not eat. So when Talha awoke he approved those who ate it and said: We ate it with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1384","Asbat narrated to us, Mutarrif narrated to us, from Amir, from Yahya ibn Talha, from his father, he said: Umar saw Talha ibn Ubayd Allah heavy, so he said: What is with you, O Abu so-and-so? Perhaps the leadership of your cousin displeased you, O Abu so-and-so? He said: No, except that I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a hadith; nothing prevented me from asking him about it except ability over it until he died. I heard him say: I know a word no servant says at his death except his color brightens for it and Allah relieves his distress. He said: So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I know what it is. He said: And what is it? He said: Do you know a word greater than a word by which he commanded his uncle at death: There is no god but Allah? Talha said: You spoke truthfully; it is, by Allah, it."
"1385","Waki narrated to us, from Ismail, he said, Qays said: I saw Talha with a paralyzed hand; with it he shielded the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of Uhud."
"1386","Ibrahim ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Salih ibn Umar narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, from Yahya ibn Talha ibn Ubayd Allah, from his father, that Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, saw him gloomy and said: What is with you, O Abu Muhammad, gloomy? Perhaps the leadership of your cousin displeased you, meaning Abu Bakr. He said: No, and he praised Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, but I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: A word no servant says at his death except Allah relieves his distress and his color brightens. So nothing prevented me from asking him about it except ability over it until he died. So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: I know it. So Talha said to him: And what is it? So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: Do you know a word greater than a word by which he commanded his uncle: There is no god but Allah? So Talha said: It is, by Allah, it."
"1387","Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Man al-Ghifari narrated to me, Dawud ibn Khalid ibn Dinar informed me, that he passed, he and a man called Abu Yusuf of Bani Taym, by Rabia ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: Abu Yusuf said to him: We find with others of hadith what we do not find with you. So he said: Indeed I have much hadith, but Rabia ibn al-Hudayr said, and he used to keep to Talha ibn Ubayd Allah, that he never heard Talha narrate from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, any hadith at all except one hadith. Rabia ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman said: I said to him: And what is it? He said: Talha said to me: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until we overlooked the lava field of Waqim. He said: So we drew near it, and there were graves at Mahniya. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, these are the graves of our brothers? He said: Graves of our companions. Then we went out until when we came to the graves of the martyrs, he said, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: These are the graves of our brothers."
"1388","Umar ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Musa ibn Talha, from his father, he said: We used to pray while animals passed before us, so we mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: Like the back of a saddle placed before one of you, then whatever passes over him does not harm him. And Umar once said: Before him."
"1389","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salama, he said: Two men of Yemen stayed with Talha ibn Ubayd Allah, then one of them was killed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then the other remained after him a year then died upon his bed. So Talha ibn Ubayd Allah was shown that the one who died upon his bed entered Paradise before the other by a while. So Talha mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: How long did he remain on earth after him? He said: A year. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He prayed one thousand eight hundred prayers and fasted Ramadan."
"1390","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from his uncle, from his father, that he heard Talha ibn Ubayd Allah say: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam? He said: Five prayers in a day and night. He said: Is aught else upon me? He said: No. And he asked him about fasting, so he said: Fasting Ramadan. He said: Is aught else upon me? He said: No. He said: And he mentioned charity. He said: Is aught else upon me? He said: No. He said: By Allah, I will neither increase upon them nor decrease from them. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He has succeeded if he spoke truthfully."
"1391","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws, he heard Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, say to Abd al-Rahman and Talha and al-Zubayr and Sad: I adjure you by Allah by whom the heaven and earth stand, and Sufyan once said: by whose permission they stand, do you know that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity? They said: O Allah, yes."
"1392","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me, from Muadh ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman al-Taymi, from his father, he said: We were with Talha ibn Ubayd Allah while in pilgrim sanctity, and a bird was gifted to him while Talha was sleeping; so among us were those who ate and among us were those who refrained. So when Talha awoke he approved those who ate it and said: We ate it with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1393","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Simak ibn Harb, from Musa ibn Talha, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked: What screens the praying one? He said: Like the back of a saddle."
"1394","Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Musa ibn Talha, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"1395","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Simak, from Musa ibn Talha, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by people at the tops of palm-trees and said: What are these doing? They said: They pollinate it, placing the male in the female. He said: I do not think that avails anything. So they were told of that and left it. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was told, so he said: If it benefits them, let them do it, for I only thought a thought, so do not hold me for thought; but when I inform you of Allah, mighty and majestic, with anything, then take it, for I will never lie upon Allah anything."
"1396","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Mujammi ibn Yahya al-Ansari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Mawhab narrated to us, from Musa ibn Talha, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how is prayer upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim; You are Praised, Glorious. And bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed the family of Ibrahim; You are Praised, Glorious."
"1397","Abu Amir narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Sufyan al-Madaini narrated to us, Bilal ibn Yahya ibn Talha ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he saw the crescent would say: O Allah, bring it upon us with blessing and faith and safety and Islam; my Lord and your Lord is Allah."
"1398","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Zaida, from Simak ibn Harb, from Musa ibn Talha, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: One of you places before him like the back of a saddle, then prays."
"1399","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Simak, that he heard Musa ibn Talha narrating from his father, he said: I passed with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among the palms of Medina, and he saw people at the tops of palms pollinating the palms, so he said: What are these doing? He said: They take from the male and put in the female, pollinating with it. So he said: I do not think that avails anything. So it reached them and they left it and came down from them, and they bore nothing that year. So that reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said: It is only a thought I thought; if it avails anything, then do it, for I am only a man like you, and thought errs and hits; but what I tell you Allah, mighty and majestic, has said, then I will never lie upon Allah."
"1400","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Musa ibn Talha, then he mentioned it."
"1401","Waki told us: Talhah ibn Yahya ibn Talhah narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, that a group of three men from Banu Udhrah came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and embraced Islam. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Who will take care of them for me. Talhah said: I will. He said: So they stayed with Talhah. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent out an expedition, and one of them went out and was martyred. He said: Then he sent out another expedition, and another of them went out in it and was martyred. He said: Then the third died on his bed. Talhah said: And I saw these three who had stayed with me in Paradise, and I saw the one who died on his bed in front of them, and I saw the one who was martyred last next to him, and I saw the one who was martyred first of them last of them. He said: And that troubled me. He said: So I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What do you find strange in that. There is no one better before Allah than a believer who lives long in Islam for his glorification and magnification and declaration of oneness."
"1402","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi told us: Al-Harith ibn Abidah told us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mujabbar narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, looked down upon those who had besieged him and greeted them, and they did not return the greeting to him. Then Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Is Talhah among the people. Talhah said: Yes. He said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return. I greet a people among whom you are and they do not reply. He said: I did reply. He said: That is not how to reply; I can hear you but you cannot make me hear, O Talhah. I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The blood of a Muslim is not lawful except for one of three: that he disbelieve after his faith, or commit adultery after having been in wedlock, or kill a soul and so be killed for it. He said: O Allah, yes. Then Uthman said Allah is Greatest, and said: By Allah, I have never denied Allah since I knew Him, nor have I committed adultery in ignorance nor in Islam, and I abandoned it in ignorance out of aversion and in Islam out of chastity, and I have never killed a soul for which my killing would be lawful."
"1403","Qutaybah ibn Said told us: Bakr ibn Mudar told us, from Ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, that two men came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and their embracing Islam was together, and one of them was more striving than his companion. Then the striving one of them raided and was martyred. Then the other remained after him for a year, then died. Talhah said: And I saw in what the sleeper sees as if I were at the gate of Paradise, and there were the two of them, and one who came out from Paradise gave permission to the one of them who died last, then he came out and gave permission to the one who was martyred. Then they both returned to me and said to me: Go back, for your time has not yet come. In the morning Talhah narrated it to the people and they were amazed at that, and that reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then he said: At which of that do you wonder. They said: O Messenger of Allah, this one was more striving, then he was martyred in the path of Allah, and this one entered Paradise before him. Then he said: Did not this one remain after him for a year. They said: Yes. And he reached Ramadan and fasted it. They said: Yes. And he prayed such and such prostrations in the year. They said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah said: Then what is between them is farther than what is between heaven and earth."
"1404","Yaqub told us: My father told us, from Ibn Ishaq: Salim ibn Abi Umayyah Abu al-Nadr told us, he said: An old man from Banu Tamim sat with me in the mosque of Basrah, with a document of his in his hand. He said: And in the time of al-Hajjaj. Then he said to me: O Abdullah, do you think this document will avail me anything with this ruler. He said: So I said: What is this document. He said: This is a document from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, which he wrote for us that no transgression be committed against us in our charities. He said: So I said: No, by Allah, I do not think it will avail you anything. And how was the story of this document. He said: I came to Madinah with my father while I was a young lad, with camels of ours to sell, and my father was a friend of Talhah ibn Ubaydullah al-Taymi. So we stayed with him, and my father said to him: Go out with me and sell these camels of mine for me. He said: Then he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has forbidden a townsman to sell for a Bedouin, but I will go out with you and sit, and you will present your camels, and if I am satisfied with the fidelity and truthfulness of a man among those who bargain with you, I will order you to sell to him. He said: So we went out to the market and stopped our backs, and Talhah sat nearby, and men bargained with us until when a man offered us what we accepted, my father said to him: Shall I conclude the sale with him. He said: Yes, I am satisfied with his fidelity for you, so sell to him. So we sold to him. When we had taken what was ours and finished our need, my father said to Talhah: Obtain for us from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a document that no transgression be committed against us in our charities. He said: Then he said: This is for you and for every Muslim. He said: Nevertheless I would like to have with me a document from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So he went out until he brought us to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, this man is from the people of the desert and a friend of ours, and he would like you to write for him a document that no transgression be committed against him in his charity. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This is for him and for every Muslim. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I would indeed like to have with me a document from you to that effect. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wrote for us this document. End of the hadith of Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, may Allah be pleased with him."
